      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/d49c1c9ab3e139158d76141b71943ff79903e87a",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "6fd6c6e2b354da5171249c00345743a67ef31efa",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/6fd6c6e2b354da5171249c00345743a67ef31efa"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 6fd6c6e2b354da5171249c00345743a67ef31efa\nparent 05bc2f53ce0cb239c17dbdd6b261bd2db7d2a940\nauthor Bruce0X <109469941+Bruce039@users.noreply.github.com> 1790667081 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790667081 -0300\n\nnet: limit relative ban times to uint32\n\nBanMan::Ban computes the ban end as GetTime() + bantime. Both setban and\n-bantime accept any int64, so a relative bantime close to INT64_MAX\noverflows there (UBSan: signed integer overflow in banman.cpp). In\npractice the result wraps negative, the ban is treated as expired, and\nit is silently dropped.\n\nLimit relative ban times to uint32 (about 136 years):\n- setban rejects a relative bantime above UINT32_MAX\n- -bantime is parsed as uint32_t, which saturates larger values",
